# sam2p — real-world examples

`sam2p` converts raster images (and can concatenate) into PDF/PostScript and
other formats, aiming for small, precise output.

## Concatenate images/PDFs into one PDF

```sh
sam2p *.pdf out.pdf
```

## Convert a single raster image to PDF

```sh
# Wrap a scan into a PDF page
sam2p receipt.png receipt.pdf

sam2p photo.jpg photo.pdf
```

## Homelab examples

```sh
# Install on OpenSUSE Tumbleweed
sudo zypper install sam2p

# Batch-wrap a folder of scanned pages, one PDF each
for f in ~/scans/*.png; do sam2p "$f" "${f%.png}.pdf"; done

# Then merge them (sam2p, or pdfunite from poppler-tools)
sam2p ~/scans/*.pdf ~/scans/combined.pdf
```

> Tip: for PDF-only merging, `pdfunite` (poppler-tools) or `pdftk` are often
> simpler; reach for sam2p when you need tight control over image-to-PDF encoding.
